<title>BELGIUM: SOLVAY HOLDS DIVIDEND, PLANS STOCK SPLIT.</title>
<headline>SOLVAY HOLDS DIVIDEND, PLANS STOCK SPLIT.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31,</p>
<p>1996 (in billions of Belgian francs unless stated):</p>
<p>    Cons net profit	  13.63  vs  12.51</p>
<p>    Net current profit     11.54  vs  12.54</p>
<p>    Net extraordinary gain  2.09  vs   0.03 loss</p>
<p>    Net dividend		 550  vs    550</p>
<p>NOTE - Solvay SA is a Belgian chemicals group. In a</p>
<p>statement about final 1996 earnings the company said it would</p>
<p>propose a 10-for-one stock split at an extraordinary general</p>
<p>shareholders meeting in June. The split should take place in</p>
<p>September 1997, it added.</p>
<p>The company provided the following breakdown of its figures:</p>
<p>    Sales		     281.97  vs 273.35</p>
<p>    of which Europe	 187     vs 184, up two percent</p>
<p>    &quot;  &quot;   Americas	  77     vs  70, up 10 percent</p>
<p>    &quot;  &quot;   U.S.		54     vs  47, up 15 percent</p>
<p>    &quot;  &quot;   Asia-Pacific    13     vs  14, down seven percent</p>
<p>    &quot;  &quot;   MidEast Africa   5     vs   5, unchanged</p>
<p>Contribution of five business units:</p>
<p>    Unit	     Sales		 EBIT*</p>
<p>    Alkalis     81.2 vs 76.9	8.8 vs 9.7</p>
<p>    Peroxygens  16.4 vs 15.8	2.2 vs 1.5</p>
<p>    Plastics    85.0 vs 87.8	3.5 vs 8.8</p>
<p>    Processing  53.1 vs 49.1	2.5 vs 0.8</p>
<p>    Health	46.2 vs 43.9	4.3 vs 3.3</p>
<p>NOTE - * EBIT: earnings before net debt expense, taxes and</p>
<p>non allocated items</p>
<p>As well as proposing a stock split, Solvay said the</p>
<p>extraordinary shareholders meeting would be asked to vote on a</p>
<p>capital increase by incorporation of 17.6 billion francs in</p>
<p>reserves. The move would take Solvay SA's capital to 50 billion</p>
<p>francs, it said, and was designed to bring capital more in line</p>
<p>with equity.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax</p>
<p>+32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
